  "articleBody": "Hiring an interior painting contractor is about much more than picking wall colors. A clear scope prevents surprise fees, missed expectations, and delayed completion dates.\n\nOverview: A quality interior paint job starts with a detailed, itemized plan covering surface repairs, prep work, and finishes.\n\nKey Benefits: A comprehensive contract ensures you get proper prep, durable topcoats, and clear timelines without cutting corners on surface cleaning or protection.\n\nProcess Breakdown:\n- Written Scope: Ensure your proposal details whether baseboards, interior doors, crown molding, and ceilings are included or billed separately.\n- Preparation Allowance: Confirm how drywall patching, sanding, and caulking will be handled before paint touches the wall.\n- Materials and Coats: Make sure the exact paint brand, product line, sheen, and number of coats are written down.\n\nReal Examples: Homeowners often assume trim is part of an interior bid, only to find the crew is strictly rolling walls. Others discover one heavy coat was applied instead of two proper coats, leading to uneven sheen and poor durability.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start: Review your home layout, list high-wear areas, and ask whether the crew handles furniture protection and masking cleanup.\n\nReach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to review your interior painting project and request a clear, written estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}